\f1\fs22 The sleek conference table of Government Square's Secure Summit Center gleamed under clinically bright lighting. CEO Dunhilton sat at its head, fingers steepled before a sour expression as Commissioner Gerry Hardman pulled up mortality projection charts on the wall display.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Initial TMinus-Virus deployment achieved seventy-two percent mortality among exposed Evolution Elvi subjects," Gerry reported, flicking through death statistics with disturbing casualness. "We projected complete elimination of the Elvi population within thirty-six days."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Excellent," declared the Director of Moral Observance, a reed-thin woman whose severe bob cut seemed to mirror her inflexible principles. "Religious contamination contained."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Except," interrupted the Director of Citizen Enhancement, a slick character whose ambitions for Gerry's position were as transparent as his hair plugs, "that's not what's happening." He pushed a tablet down the table toward Dunhilton. "Death rates among the Elvi have been plummeting for the past seventy-two hours. Almost to zero."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Dunhilton's eyebrows contracted. "Explain."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"I can't," Gerry admitted, his professional demeanour cracking slightly. "The virus is genetically targeted. There should be no recovery."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Perhaps I can illuminate this situation," the Director of Moral Observance offered, pressing a button on her console. The wall display shifted to surveillance footage that made several cabinet members choke on their sparkling water.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The footage showed the interior of what had once been the Memphis Mafia Bar, now filled with Elvi engaged in activities that could charitably be described as "enthusiastically communal."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"What in the name of tax-deductible charity am I watching?" Dunhilton demanded.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"They're calling it 'The Humpening,'" Moral Observance explained, her voice clinically detached. "It began approximately five days ago and has spread to every Elvi enclave in the country."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Dunhilton waved dismissively. "Hardly surprising behaviour from sequin-addicted gyrators devoted to pelvic thrusting and musical indecency. The Elvi have always been morally suspect. That's why we're eliminating them."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Sir," Gerry interjected, "there's more." He brought up a new set of surveillance images showing Sarah Jacobson\'97visibly pregnant\'97entering Elvi Parliament with Dr. Katherine Logan and Detective Superintendent Hayley Lanning. "This visit occurred precisely twelve hours before the... activity... began escalating exponentially."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"The Holy Momma," whispered the Commissioner of Elvi Rights, recognition dawning.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Gerry continued, displaying a timeline of Sarah's movements from Sublime Point to Elvi Parliament to Starborne One. "After these visits, we observed a 600% increase in... social activity... among the Elvi population. More importantly, previously infected Elvi began showing complete recovery."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"This is," the Director of Tourism contributed, "possibly the most disgusting public health initiative in recorded history."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The Refrigeration Ombudsman, whose presence at security briefings remained mysteriously persistent, cleared his throat. "My sources in cold storage logistics report unprecedented demand for ice and cooling products in the Quarter. Apparently, they're using the walk-in freezers for... alternative purposes."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Can we focus?" Dunhilton snapped. "Commissioner Hardman, are you suggesting that Ms. Jacobson is somehow neutralising our virus through... organised debauchery?"\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"That's exactly what I'm saying." Gerry rose, circling the table slowly. "Everyone out except Directors Freedom and Health."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The room cleared reluctantly, with the Director of Citizen Enhancement shooting Gerry a glare that promised future repercussions.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>When only three remained, Gerry turned to Dunhilton. "Sir, I believe we're dealing with a counter-agent. The TPlus-Virus."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"The what?" Dunhilton demanded.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"A classified file from HIBReLabs. Health remembers it, don't you?" Gerry nodded to the wizened Director of Health, who looked distinctly uncomfortable. "A virus that enhances cellular regeneration, provides immune system superiority, and\'97most critically\'97spreads through bodily fluids."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Jamison Hardy's pet project," Health admitted reluctantly. "Deemed too dangerous and unpredictable. All samples were supposedly destroyed."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Evidently not all of them," Gerry said grimly. "I believe Anthony Chantara\'97the Elvi's 'Great Teacher'\'97is carrying the virus. The Elvi have weaponised promiscuity as a delivery system."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Who would have authorised\'97" Dunhilton began, then stopped, realisation dawning. "Eloise."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"The timing fits," Gerry confirmed. "Hardy was in Shakti custody. Sarah Jacobson is married to Alexander Shakti. The TPlus-Virus emerges just as our TMinus-Virus strikes."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Dunhilton's face darkened to a dangerous shade of crimson. "She's undermining our biological solution with her own biological solution. Using my own godson as patient zero!"\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"It's worse," Gerry said quietly. "My sources suggest the Elvi are preparing for a major concert event\'97'Rock Against Revival.' Given current transmission patterns, I project complete immunity among Elvi populations within fourteen days."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Dunhilton slammed his fist on the table, sending water glasses trembling. "She's gone too far this time. Shakti thinks she can play god with weapons tech, sabotage government operations, and turn my own family against me?"\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>He stood, straightening his tie with deadly precision. "Gentlemen, we are now at war with Sublime Point. I want every available asset mobilised. We'll make an example of Eloise Shakti that this country won't soon forget."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>As Gerry left to implement the orders, he couldn't suppress a small smile. The wheels he'd set in motion months ago were finally turning at full speed. Whether Dunhilton or Eloise emerged victorious hardly mattered\'97Gerry Hardman's own contingency plans were already well underway.
